#C The patterns in this collection hassle common predecessors of the
#C traffic light constellation. There is an unusual proliferation of
#C oscillators engineered this way due to the traffic light's high 
#C level of symmetry and the frequency with which it occurs naturally.
#C
#C This collection is split into two parts:
#C  * The top contains standard traffic light hasslers.
#C  * The bottom contains "pre-pulsar" hasslers.
#C A pre-pulsar is a pair of pre-traffic lights whose centers are
#C 5 cells apart.  If left to evolve, they would not form traffic
#C lights, but would instead form the period-3 pulsar oscillator.
#C
#C An example is given at most periods for which a traffic light
#C hassler is known.  Some periods have only been achieved through
#C the extensible traffic jam reaction (demonstrated here only at
#C p110).  These periods are not included here, but can be found at
#C https://conwaylife.com/wiki/Traffic_jam
#C
#C For discovery credits and additional traffic light hasslers, visit
#C https://conwaylife.com/wiki/Traffic_light_hasslers
#C https://conwaylife.com/wiki/Pre-pulsar_hasslers
#C https://conwaylife.com/wiki/Pre-pulsar_shuttles
